Reason (2026-11-11, Nam: "co, viet patch" — let the eval runner use offline `pls`):
The P2 evals of 2026-11-11 (`evals/results/pls-p2-solution-designer/2026-11-11-v07.md`) could not
exercise `pls xref` (P2 step 5, since 0.6) or `pls lint` (step 9): `pls-x-eval-case-runner` has no shell.
This patch does NOT give the runner Bash. Claude Code's `tools:` field takes bare tool names only (no
`Bash(cmd:*)` specifier is documented), and a settings `deny` rule "isn't a security boundary"
(`python3 …`, `bash -c …` slip past) — official docs sub-agents.md / permissions.md, checked 2026-11-11.
A runner with Bash could run `pls` against dev with the operator's credentials, and the hook that would
make an allowlist hard (TD-21) does not exist yet. Instead the runner names the command under
`COMMAND TO RUN:` and the Orchestrator runs it after checking it against the local-only list — the same
relay as for the person role in interview cases (`evals/README.md`). The relayer runs the framework's own
`tools/pls/pls.py` with `python -I`, never a file from the scratch folder, which the runner can write
(review 2026-11-11, `plans/2026-11-11-eval-runner-local-pls/review.md`). Apply with `git apply`.

